  {
   "id": "ShDeZux9tAEJ",
   "from": "Greg",
   "author": "5cdc3cec34f427f1",
   "date": "2014-01-29T22:52:05Z",
   "subject": "Error with \"curve\" command",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I&#39;m trying to adapt Dave Harris&#39;s code on maximum likelihood estimation for one of my models, and I&#39;m running into trouble with the &quot;curve&quot; command. I don&#39;t get any errors when I define the function I want to evaluate, but then when I try to plot lines using this new function I get the following error:<br><br>Error in curve(SAR(x, M = 0.6, a = 1), add = TRUE, from = 0, to = 20) : <br>  &#39;expr&#39; did not evaluate to an object of length &#39;n&#39;<br>In addition: Warning message:<br>In Strikes * M/(a + strikes) :<br>  longer object length is not a multiple of shorter object length<br><br>I have attached my code (gnl parameter estimation) and my data set. Please let me know if anybody has any thoughts. Thanks<br><br>Greg<br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "BSbEfU5VucYJ",
   "from": "Noam Ross",
   "author": "8c8f0ca54c4a2459",
   "date": "2014-01-30T00:05:17Z",
   "subject": "Re: [D-RUG]: Error with \"curve\" command",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-size:1em;font-family:Helvetica,arial,freesans,clean,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);background-color:rgb(255,255,255);border:none;line-height:1.2\">\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">Hi Greg,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">In the file you attached, your <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline\">SAR</code> function uses <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline\">Strikes</code> and <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline\">strikes</code> inconsistently.  R is case-sensitive so it’s looking for two variables:</p>\r\n\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;overflow:auto;margin:1em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background-color:rgb(248,248,255);background-repeat:initial initial\">SAR = function(Strikes, M, a) {\r\n    Strikes*M/(a + strikes)\r\n}</code></pre>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">When I run the file I get this different error:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;overflow:auto;margin:1em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background-color:rgb(248,248,255);background-repeat:initial initial\">Error in SAR(x, M = 0.8, a = 3) : object &#39;strikes&#39; not found</code></pre>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">When I changed the last <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline\">strikes</code> in the function to <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline\">Strikes</code>, everything worked fine.  I suspect that you had a value for <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline\">strikes</code> somewhere in your environment which obscured this error.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">Vince will not forgive me if I don’t also point out that using <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline\">attach</code> is often problematic because for just this reason - you end up with variables in your environment that are difficult to track.  Better to refer to the data frame directly (<code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline\">data$Rep</code>) or wrap your code in a <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline\">with()</code> function.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">Noam</p>\r\n</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Jan 29, 2014 at 2:52 PM, Greg <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">grey...@ucdavis.edu</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n</div></div>"
